            <ArticleTitle>Case report: intravenous etidronate as a cause of poor uptake on bone scanning, with a review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>268-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bone scanning is the most frequent type of radionuclide examination performed. We present a case of reduced uptake on a bone scan thought to be due to etidronate therapy. Other causes of this phenomenon are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
